    {
      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_HrServ-webshell-in-APT-attack(11-22-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s1"
      },
      "text": "securelist.com /hrserv-apt-web-shell/111119 Mert Degirmenci In the course of our routine investigation, we discovered a DLL file, identified as hrserv.dll, which is a previously unknown web shell exhibiting sophisticated features such as custom encoding methods for client communication and in-memory execution.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_HrServ-webshell-in-APT-attack(11-22-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "Initial infection According to our telemetry data, the PAExec.exe process initiates the creation of a scheduled task on the system named MicrosoftsUpdate (sic), which in turn is designed to execute a .BAT file.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_HrServ-webshell-in-APT-attack(11-22-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s2"
      },
      "text": "HrServ then initiates an HTTP server utilizing the HTTP server API for its functionality.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_19",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_HrServ-webshell-in-APT-attack(11-22-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "As a result, the registry and the temporary file are used as a communication channel between the implant and HrServ.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_23",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_HrServ-webshell-in-APT-attack(11-22-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s2"
      },
      "text": "Attribution The TTPs analyzed in this investigation are not associated with any known threat actors we are tracking, but there are a few things that we observed: the GET parameters used in the hrserv.dll file, which is used to mimic Google services, include “hl”.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_31",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Kaspersky_HrServ-webshell-in-APT-attack(11-22-2023)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "rule",
        "sentence_id": "p1_r1"
      },
      "text": "In the course of our routine investigation, we discovered a DLL file, identified as hrserv.dll, which is a previously unknown web shell exhibiting sophisticated features such as custom encoding methods for client communication and in-memory execution. Our analysis of the sample led to the discovery of related variants compiled in 2021, indicating a potential correlation between these separate occurrences of malicious activity.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "note": "rule or indicator snippet evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
